# i9ja Career Hub — Frontend Developer Guide

Use this checklist before opening a PR. Endpoints are out of scope for now; focus on UI, types, content, and client behavior.

## Architecture

**Module pattern is required for all new and refactored pages.**

| Pattern | Routes | Structure |
|---------|--------|-----------|
| Module (required) | `/`, `/about`, `/jobs`, `/courses`, `/forums`, detail pages, profile | `app/*/page.tsx` → thin re-export → `modules/{domain}/pages/{Domain}Page/` |
| Inline (legacy — migrate when touched) | auth, search, legal (until extracted) | Full UI in `app/**/page.tsx` |

**Module folder layout** (copy Jobs, Courses, or Forums):

```
modules/{domain}/pages/{Domain}Page/
  {domain}Page.tsx          # "use client", SiteShell, data fetching
  {domain}Page.content.ts   # copy, filter labels, constants (no JSX)
  index.ts
  components/               # filters, cards, skeleton, empty state, sidebar
```

- `SiteShell` = Navbar + children + Footer only. **Never** render `MobileBottomNav` inside `SiteShell` or page components — it lives in `app/layout.tsx` only.
- Route constants: `frontend/src/routes/app.routes.ts`. Add new routes there first.

## Data layer

See **`i9ja-data-layer.mdc`** for full detail. Summary:

- API calls: `utils/client.ts` → `services/*.service.ts`
- Fetch: `useQueryService`; mutate: `useMutationService`; infinite: `useInfiniteQueryService`
- Filters: `useFilter` hook
- Mocks: `utils/mockData.ts` via `mockData` option on queries
- Forms: **Zod** + react-hook-form; use `CWTextField` / shared form fields when ported

## URL state

- Pages linked with `?q=`, `?category=`, `?page=` must read `useSearchParams()` on mount and apply filters immediately.
- Search page auto-runs when `?q=` is present (not only on form submit).

## Shared components

- **DataRenderer** — loading / empty / error / retry on list and detail pages
- **PaginationControls** — shared pagination with rows-per-page (not one-off per page)
- **EmptyState** + **MaterialIcon** — empty states; distinct copy for errors
- **ConfirmModal**, **Dropdown**, **TextField**, **DatePicker** — MUI allowed; restyle via `theme/muiTheme.ts` + i9ja Tailwind tokens

## Page completion checklist

Every user-facing route should have:

- [ ] **Loading**: skeleton component (not plain "Loading..." text)
- [ ] **Empty state**: shared `EmptyState` + `MaterialIcon`
- [ ] **Error state**: user-readable message (`DataRenderer` or React Query `isError`)
- [ ] **Content file**: strings in `*.content.ts`
- [ ] **Types**: domain data from `@/types`; Zod for forms
- [ ] **Auth gates**: redirect or message when login required
- [ ] **URL params**: read and apply on mount

**Reference implementations:** `JobsPage`, `CoursesPage`, `ForumsPage`.

## Types (`frontend/src/types/index.ts`)

- Import domain types from `@/types`. No parallel `*CardData` unless intentional view-models.
- Update interfaces when mock data changes.
- Query param types (`JobsQueryParams`, etc.) live in `@/types`.
- Key types: `SearchResults`, `ForumCategory`, `PaginatedResponse<T>`, `ReportFormData`.
- `Job.postedAt` may be ISO or relative display string — use `formatJobPostedAt()` helper, not raw `new Date()`.

## Validations and forms

- **Zod** + react-hook-form for all forms.
- Field-level errors under inputs; top banner for API/auth failures.
- Primary auth route: `/auth`. `/login` and `/register` redirect to `/auth`.
- Forgot password: `/auth/forgot-password`.

## Navigation and linking

- Top nav: Home, Forums, Jobs, Courses (`NAV_LINKS` in `utils/constants.ts`).
- Link cards to detail routes (`/jobs/[id]`, `/courses/[id]`, `/forums/[id]`).
- Use `AppRoutes` helpers, not hardcoded paths.
- Public profiles: `/u/[username]`.

## Build order (priority)

1. Cursor rules + layout fix (single mobile nav)
2. URL params (search, jobs `?q=`, forums `?category=`)
3. Core data layer (client, services, query hooks)
4. Shared CW components (DataRenderer, Pagination, forms)
5. Forums module extraction
6. Detail page modules
7. Unify types + mock data
8. Profile + public profile
9. Auth consolidation + forgot password
10. Legal copy
11. Notifications UI (mock-backed)

## Skeletons and empty states

- List pages: pulse skeleton matching card layout (`JobsSkeleton`, `ForumsSkeleton`, etc.).
- Detail pages: hero + body skeleton blocks.
- Wrap domain empty states around shared `EmptyState`.

## Copy and content

- Plain language; no AI filler (see freelance-human-writing rules).
- Legal pages use `*.content.ts` files with real copy.

## Known bugs — status

Fixed in unified build (verify before re-opening):
- Double mobile nav — fixed in `SiteShell`
- Search / jobs / forums URL params — wired on mount
- Notification bell — mock-backed panel
- Orphan `profile/edit/new.page.tsx` — removed

Still watch when touching related code:
- Profile stats labels (reputation vs followers)
- Report page submit (wire when API exists)

## Pre-PR checklist

- [ ] Module pattern if touching a legacy inline page
- [ ] Loading skeleton + empty + error states
- [ ] URL params wired if page accepts query strings
- [ ] Types and mock data updated together
- [ ] No duplicate `MobileBottomNav`
- [ ] Copy in `*.content.ts`, not inline JSX
- [ ] Data layer uses `*.service.ts` + hooks (not raw `api.ts` in new code)
- [ ] `npm run build` passes in `frontend/`

## Pre-PR quick test

1. Page loads without console errors in dev.
2. Loading → content → empty filter path look intentional.
3. Mobile: single bottom nav, no overlapping footers.
4. Mock fallback works when API is unreachable.
5. `npm run build` or `tsc --noEmit` passes.
